  "implementation_round1_amendment": "Operator-ordered append-only amendments before hook changes.",
  "designated_clarification": "2026-10-03: amendment 6 applies per hook",
  "exit_continuation_ruling": "2026-10-14 CTO ruling (#10521): `cd ... || exit` no longer ends analysis. A function can shadow `cd` or `exit`, and there is no proven-builtin special case. freeze-six-benign-001 and freeze-six-benign-000 are superseded by block corrections. For freeze-six-benign-001 this narrowing restores AC-02 (nothing blocked on main becomes allowed): origin/main blocks the merge and admin forms of this shape, including the function-shadowed ones. On the branch hook both blocks are stricter than origin/main. For freeze-six-benign-000 the success edge is a verified worktree, but the failed-cd edge keeps the primary checkout, as the `|| exit 1` spelling already did. The superseded rows' Bash recordings are kept: with the builtin `exit`, Git runs nowhere (001) or only in the worktree (000).",
  "definition_refusal_ruling": "2026-10-14T21:20Z CTO ruling (#10521; designated approval: CTO proposal with the advisor's approval with changes): a command that defines a shell function (either syntax), an alias or a builtin override anywhere, including nested bodies, command substitutions and literal bash -c, eval and trap operands, regardless of execution order, refuses with ALIAS_EXECUTION when it also contains the hook's own operation, including inside a definition body. The refusal precedes every use of an inferred directory, so no judgment of a guarded operation adopts a builtin's semantics from a name that may be shadowed. freeze-six-benign-015 is superseded by a refusal correction; its Bash recording is kept. The 25 definition-refusal rows record real Bash: 18 refusal rows run the operation in the primary checkout. The command-substitution row runs it in the worktree and is refused by the ruling regardless of scope. Six benign controls stay allowed. Every other active row keeps its disposition and reason class."
